{"baseRefName":"main","headRefName":"feat/sou-67-generalized-constrained-tool-bindings","headRefOid":"59bb5dfda3e326d314ac8f1a8a67222d9fa8229d","isDraft":false,"mergeStateStatus":"BEHIND","mergeable":"MERGEABLE","number":161,"reviewDecision":"CHANGES_REQUESTED","reviews":[{"id":"PRR_kwDOUQDdVs8AAAABSz319w","author":{"login":"winux125"},"authorAssociation":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"Changes requested: the current diff is a useful name-alias increment, but does not yet deliver the SOU-67 binding contract described in the issue/PR completion claim.\n\nIndependent exact-head offline build and both new tests passed. An additional production-parser witness confirmed that a bounded original create schema with a nested destination path is accepted by InputSchema::read but rejected by NativeState::from_bytes as invalid operator create-file policy. The unchanged exact create_file_schema digest and /path checks still enforce the old fixed argument shape.\n\nPlease add the separate additive, versioned original-tool binding and validator required by SOU-67: explicit operation, path/content selectors (including the supported direct/nested forms), supported response contract, executor identity and limits; derive and bind any internal projection to the original admitted arguments without renaming or rewriting the host frame. Reject ambiguous/overlapping selectors, unsupported extra effects and schema drift. Preserve the legacy profiles and current confinement/Ask/Deny/receipt limits.\n\nThe new read test proves an actual custom-name read and zero child dispatch. The create test proves native authorization only: it ends after release/binding assertions and does not run the actual collector or inspect a created file. Before marking this delivered, add an owned collector create/refusal demo with actual filesystem and hostile-child witnesses plus the required replay, no-overwrite, replacement/symlink, cancellation and post-commit withholding controls. Include operator migration/support notes and exact-source evidence; none are added in this PR.\n\nKeep SOU-67 In Progress and remove the completion claim until the full scoped delivery is reviewable. No approval or merge while these gaps and current-head CI/security checks remain.","submittedAt":"2026-10-17T10:03:05Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"reactionGroups":[],"state":"CHANGES_REQUESTED","commit":{"oid":"59bb5dfda3e326d314ac8f1a8a67222d9fa8229d"}}],"state":"OPEN","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","conclusion":"","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/SoupTeam/soup-wall/actions/runs/39023067357/job/117368583178","name":"Linux dependency alerts and protected durable recovery","startedAt":"2026-10-17T09:57:33Z","status":"IN_PROGRESS","workflowName":"protected-alert-recovery"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-10-17T09:58:12Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/SoupTeam/soup-wall/actions/runs/39023066268/job/117368582188","name":"Analyze (actions)","startedAt":"2026-10-17T09:57:33Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"CodeQL"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-10-17T10:02:54Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/SoupTeam/soup-wall/actions/runs/39023067344/job/117368583160","name":"linux-https-get","startedAt":"2026-10-17T09:57:33Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Constrained MCP HTTPS GET"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-10-17T10:02:44Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/SoupTeam/soup-wall/actions/runs/39023067283/job/117368583189","name":"linux-create-file","startedAt":"2026-10-17T09:57:33Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Constrained MCP file creation"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-10-17T10:02:58Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/SoupTeam/soup-wall/actions/runs/39023067363/job/117368583254","name":"owned-recovery","startedAt":"2026-10-17T09:57:33Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Encrypted Console recovery"